Connect an assembly prediction to a bounded inspection decision (@engineering-decision-evidence: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Investigate-an-assembly-from-views-to-dimensional-evidence.lingua#r_0389B90567C4C9183DE77AC20A") { r_0AE23276AAB728BEDBFC0AC47E
A geometrical model predicts a property under its assumptions. An observation estimates a defined property of a particular object under a procedure. A specification states an allowed region, and a decision rule connects evidence to a declared conclusion. Reuse [Begin with a question and specify the measurand](../../inquiry/metrology/foundations/Question-and-measurand.lingua#r_7ZNCJFEGXNJSGJJJKGYH6MGFE6), [Principle, method, procedure, indication, and result](../../inquiry/metrology/foundations/Principle-procedure-result.lingua#r_2PT30AZGBV9V63Z3T0G7W8FSP6) and [Separate observed variation from uncertainty about a result](../../inquiry/core/Separate-observed-variation-from-uncertainty-about-a-result.lingua#r_0A1A2CA3D01039474C1F5678C7) rather than treating these as interchangeable numbers.

For the tray, specify whether g means the longitudinal separation of two associated parallel reference planes, a local contact measurement at a stated location, or the minimum opening over the relevant interface. A tapered or misaligned real gap can make these different quantities. Specify reference conditions, alignment, contact, access and treatment of surface form before choosing an instrument. Reading one point cannot by itself establish every position or prove the ideal-plane model adequate. The shared dimensional-measurement lesson supplies that practical bridge.

Use a deliberately bounded teaching rule. Suppose a synthetic reading r is known, under an explicitly assumed error model, to satisfy |r−g|≤u, with u≥0. Here u is a stipulated hard error bound, not a standard uncertainty or a 95% coverage interval. The compatible values form [r−u,r+u]. For the inclusive allowed region [0.90,1.10] mm, call the result within only if the entire compatible interval lies inside; outside only if it is disjoint; otherwise unresolved. These labels refer to this teaching model and rule. They are not a claim of conformity under a current industrial standard.

For r=1.04 mm and u=0.03 mm, the compatible interval is [1.01,1.07] mm and the result is within. At r=1.09 with the same u it is [1.06,1.12], so the result is unresolved even though the reading lies inside the specified region. At r=1.15 it is [1.12,1.18], so the result is outside. A compatible interval that merely touches an allowed endpoint is not disjoint: r=0.87, u=0.03 gives [0.84,0.90] and remains unresolved. Endpoints matter when the requirement is inclusive.

Real uncertainty evaluations rarely supply an absolute bound on all errors. A coverage interval and an acceptance rule involve stated probability and risk assumptions, which require later formation. Do not convert a standard uncertainty into a guaranteed interval or assume a multiplier always means a fixed coverage probability. The historical NPL Guide 79 inspection discussion supports asking how uncertainty affects interpretation; its quoted standard editions and numerical heuristics are not adopted here as a current normative rule.

**Work:** construct the decision regions as r varies for fixed u, including u=0 and an interval too wide to fit inside the permitted region. Explain why narrowing u may resolve a result but cannot repair a gap actually outside specification. Describe which evidence could invalidate the hard-bound assumption, and what further observations are needed for unmeasured form or condition changes. Retain raw readings, model assumptions, reference conditions and revisions through [Report a result so its uncertainty survives later use](../../inquiry/metrology/uncertainty/Reporting-and-use.lingua#r_1DX8JW7A1K3R87MJ4W9AYVJ52D) and [Connect realization to verification and intended use](Connect-realization-to-verification-and-intended-use.lingua#r_0C593F4A7A204FABB3B5876653). A reproducible calculation does not turn hypothetical inputs into physical measurements.

**Reading companion:** [Engineering drawings for measurement — NPL Guide 79](../mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design/sources/Engineering-Drawings-for-Measurement-NPL.lingua#r_48E0H38P8GEB0XPX68MYXGGA48), printed pages 22–27, 40–41 and the bounded inspection discussion on 70–74. Keep historical convention/uncertainty language distinct from a current normative deliverable. The shared measurement sources supply deeper definitions.

**Continue:** [Investigate an assembly from views to dimensional evidence](Investigate-an-assembly-from-views-to-dimensional-evidence.lingua#r_0389B90567C4C9183DE77AC20A).

**Return:** [Engineering](../Engineering.lingua#r_5DA6VY09MAD2N8D9SH0FFJVV68).
